WEBVTT

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.570
You guys are pathetic!

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:11.350
Women don't like guys with such low stamina!

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.370
Piss off. Don't go comparing us to a freak like you.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.250
Aren't you all frustrated that a dainty
little gal like me stole your thunder?

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.070
"Gal" my ass, you 25-year-old midget!

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.900
25 years old.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.280
Still. Makes. Me. A.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.600
A y-y-y-young—

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.740
Hm?

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:40.600
A young lady!

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.030
Nike!

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.080
My ear! My ear!

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.250
I was so scared, Colonel! Really, really scared!

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.110
But I tried my absolute hardest!

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.500
I-Indeed. Good work.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.540
Are you proud? Am I a good girl?

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.200
Yes, of course.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.730
You took an enemy General's head.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:06.460
Once we return, I'm certain you'll be
awarded a medal of honor for your achievements.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.820
Then... Can I have my usual reward?

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.840
I wanna be praised by you Colonel, even more than
Secretary General Loquis or General Borcuse.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:22.590
Pardon me, Colonel.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.230
We did receive permission to rest, but is it really
prudent to do so in the middle of enemy territory?

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.290
It's fine. The general's forces are
keeping watch for us, so rest assured.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:37.330
We've been marching for 25 hours
straight. I imagine we're at our limits.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:41.590
It will likely take about six hours for the
enemy remnants to retreat to their army.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.890
You have precisely four hours to rest!

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.020
After that, we resume our attack.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.500
That's the signal from our scouts!

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.880
Athens forces spotted! Estimated 50 units!

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:42.180
50 Golems?! That's 20 less than we've got!

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.790
Captain Elsa! Let's swarm the enemy!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.070
Restrain yourself!

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.180
Wait for General Baldr's orders!

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.260
Prepare to intercept them with your Pressure Guns!

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.590
We've got the high ground!
Do not leave your positions!

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:56.670
Yes sir!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.590
Krisnan forces spotted. Approximately 70 in number.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:10.270
They're in perfect position to meet our attack.
Impressive as usual, General Baldr.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:13.940
Charge.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.150
All units, commence operation!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:20.720
Fire!

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.280
They're attempting a Pincer?

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.030
General, Captain Elsa, over there!

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.790
You can see from here? Is that really him?!

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:49.790
Yes. It distinctly resembles the Commander's
Golem that we spotted crossing the border.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:50.740
Impossible...

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.670
General Baldr.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:58.220
Forget it, Elsa. It's a blatant challenge!

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.970
Yes, I believe it is.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:00.660
However...

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:05.150
Staring each other down like
this could cost us valuable time.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.060
If we don't act now, we'll never have a chance like this again.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:12.980
Please lend me 10 Golems before their reinforcements arrive.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.880
Alright. Take 20.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:23.330
But you're to retreat immediately at the first sign of danger!

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:24.800
Understood?

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.200
Yes sir!

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.740
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.010
All units, open fire!

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.380
<i>What a spectacular attack.</i>

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:05.340
<i>A classic blitz maneuver.</i>

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:15.850
<i>However, your misdirected attack
didn't turn out like you had expected.</i>

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:24.570
<i>Such is war. Your carefully
calculated decision has backfired.</i>

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:39.460
<i>A clear head can be just as much of a hindrance.</i>

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.500
<i>A lesson you've just learned the hard way.</i>

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.710
E-Elsa squad... annihilated.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:05.560
A mere six golems defeated Elsa <i>and</i> 20 of ours!

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:10.810
A-And Athens' didn't reform their ranks!

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:14.630
Those bastards didn't even bother protecting their commander!

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:17.760
<i>No, they didn't.</i>

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:20.770
<i>They simply stood by... and watched our jaws drop.</i>

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:27.020
<i>Elsa losing to a mere six golems and
the bizarre actions of their flanks...</i>

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.140
<i>It's no wonder the men are terrified.</i>

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:35.520
<i>Borcuse... Did you plan to gamble
for this outcome from the start?</i>

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.880
<i>Fear deals a crippling blow to soldiers.</i>

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:43.800
<i>Be it a single man or a force of one
million soldiers, it makes no difference.</i>

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.670
<i>Man can't deny neither hunger nor fear.</i>

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.440
Nike. You may begin.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:54.340
Yes, but sir...

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:59.510
General, I do not feel that such actions are necessary!

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.470
They are.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:03.010
Do it, Nike.

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:05.760
Sorry, Colonel.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:11.110
Oh well, she's already dead anyway.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.890
Technically, you could just call this disassembly!

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.180
Borcuse...

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:29.800
That's Captain Elsa's...

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.700
Captain Elsa...

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:49.270
Your men are panicking.

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.850
And you'll come under fire
whether you charge or retreat.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:57.100
At this juncture, it's already checkmate for you.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:02.380
Forgive me, Elsa.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.980
All units, charge!

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:11.910
Did I stutter? All golems, prepare to attack!

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.840
Reconnaissance, Supply Teams and Infantry, standby!

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:16.620
Kill every last enemy before you!

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.790
B-But sir, the enemy's...

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.120
Alright! Let's move!

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:23.540
Y-Yes sir!

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.720
Roger!

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:28.600
Let's take back the Captain's remains!

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.460
They've rallied their spirits.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.010
Victory is officially ours.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.050
Perhaps.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:42.710
However, the soldiers' fear has transformed into rage.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:45.890
They'll likely fight to their dying breath.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:51.820
General Baldr, you're so
straightforward it makes me sick.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:56.430
Moving to intercept.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:10:01.070
Colonel Io. We'll continue our discussion later.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:04.350
I appreciate your concern, but I have no need for it.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:05.680
Move out!

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:06.510
Roger!

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.820
What the fuck is our left flank doing!?

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:21.250
Just ignore their rear guard!

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.850
At this rate, we can't link up with the right flank!

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.610
We'll make a detour and pursue the enemy's main forces!

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:33.280
Borcuse!

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:50.070
God dammit! We're not finished yet, Athens!

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:52.250
Bolster your defenses! Here they come!

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:53.900
Alright, fire!

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.610
Don't retreat! Just leave it to the rear support!

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:06.510
Not yet! Hold on a little longer!

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.280
They're holding out pretty well!

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:12.060
I'm gonna earn myself a medal today!

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.030
F-Fire!

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.380
General Baldr! The enemy's left side ceased their attack!

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:52.100
Is it Rygart?

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.540
The left side's being decimated by the enemy!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:57.440
Dammit, left flank! Get it together!

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:00.360
Just... one hostile?

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.150
Ah, it is indeed a single unit.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:07.050
Hmph. Krisna certainly has
some interesting characters.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:11.800
Bardess! What kind of man laughs as he watches his comrades die?

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:14.570
Sir! I was merely laughing at my own comment.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:18.250
I'm terribly sorry, General Borcuse.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.570
Do you understand, Rygart?

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:24.340
Once the third layer of armor's been compromised,

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.560
you may treat it as if the frame itself has been damaged.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:29.170
At that point, you're to purge the armor and withdraw.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:32.420
I'm already down to my last layer.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:36.550
But... I have no choice!

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:39.440
I have to become a cold-blooded killer!

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.040
He stopped me!

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.120
Fire!

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:04.600
Dammit! Purge or not,
the armor's not gonna last any longer!

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.640
W-What the hell kind of jump is that!?

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.860
Guard your vital points and close the distance!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.610
Shit, the nail darts aren't cutting it.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.280
Just piercing them isn't good enough.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:30.030
Aim for his landing point!

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.410
Scatter! We're being sniped!

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.140
That's enough, Rygart! Now fall back!

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:48.870
Hey Narvi, that tremor just now was from the Delphine's landing!

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.050
They've already started!

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:53.390
We were supposed to initiate the attack...

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:57.510
Loggin and Rygart's team had more
distance to cover. Just what <i>is</i> that golem?

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.150
Nyle, enemy spotted!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.180
Right!

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:06.180
We can't pull off a rear attack,
but we can come in from the side!

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:09.100
Looks like 23 units out there. You sure about this?

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:13.540
Of course! While Baldr acts as a decoy, our squad will take them down!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:17.230
It's the ideal situation. I can make
a splendid report to General True!

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:18.400
Begin the attack!

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.390
Girghe!? What the hell are you doing?

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:25.380
I said begin the attack!

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:29.540
Girghe!

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:35.280
I can't do it.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:37.340
What?

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:41.280
My legs are cramping. I can't move!

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:45.080
I... I'm scared!

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:49.290
I've never fought in real combat before!

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:58.810
Excellent work, Rygart.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:04.040
The enemy's left formation has collapsed.
General Baldr's forces have begun regrouping.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:12.720
This thing's only got six minutes of juice left.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.690
Is this your idea of a joke, Girghe!?

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.880
You're <i>scared</i> !?

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:23.310
Since when have you been such a spineless pansy?

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.070
Yeah, c'mon man.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.960
Show us that same strength you tried to kill us with!

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:30.000
More like we're screwed if you don't...

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:35.900
T-That was during training!
I knew the exact number of enemies!

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:39.020
And besides, that was just a mock battle!

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.780
We're in trouble, Narvi! The enemy's spotted us!

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:49.640
Our surprise attack's a bust. Should we retreat?

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:54.520
No, the enemy's still disorganized! You and I can still break through!

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.970
Baldr's already noticed us and begun moving!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.710
We'll launch a pincer attack!

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:00.060
Move out!

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:01.810
Roger that!

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:14.240
<i>A golem with a broken blade for
a horn that disrupted our tactics...</i>

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:20.680
<i>It's a complete mystery to us,
but it's power and mobility are astounding.</i>

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:23.910
<i>I guess I could call it the Broken Blade for the time being.</i>

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.120
That's... Borcuse?

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:36.730
Colonel, the enemy's retreating!

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:38.200
Damn you, Baldr.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.890
He was trying to lure us out.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:44.610
We can't just watch our right flank be killed.
Very well. You may join them!

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:46.080
Yes sir!

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.230
Colonel Io, wait!

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:53.210
It is time.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:01.600
Aw man, the withdrawal signal?

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:04.720
You're mine!

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:11.950
Two down!

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:17.680
All that's left is for Nyle and I to crush the right flank!

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.620
Didn't quite go according to plan though.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:20.620
Perfect!

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:25.140
Huh?

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:29.380
Nobody's here.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:35.460
Seems like Baldr's team's in pursuit,

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.980
but they're way ahead of us now.

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:41.400
The enemy... retreated?

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:46.260
Dammit! We're late!

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.040
Is he running away?

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:07.320
Forget it. Once you drop down to five minutes,
you could run out out of power while in enemy range.

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:11.100
<i>Do not</i> join the pursuit teams.

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:16.810
Why do I feel relieved?

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.080
A-Are you okay?

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.300
Haven't slept in three days, that's all.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:39.130
Attach segment 5-86 with the new rivets...

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:44.070
Cleo... help me swap out these parts...

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:46.290
Oh, you mean help you get changed?

00:18:58.600 --> 00:18:59.710
Thanks.

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:04.480
What beautiful, black hair...

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:10.700
I think blonde hair is prettier.

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:12.680
You really... think... so?

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:19.340
Untainted by any other shade. Purely black...

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:23.390
Personally, I... truly admire it.

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:33.990
<i>She's Zess' friend, just like that man Rygart.</i>

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:35.900
<i>But she's still my enemy.</i>

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:38.710
<i>I don't understand.</i>

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:45.530
Retreating while we were
crushing them? What a load of crap.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:48.450
Nike, this is a strategic withdrawal.

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:51.490
We're merely going to join up with the
rear guard and some reinforcements.

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:57.070
"Strategic withdrawal". That's such a convenient phrase, isn't it?

00:19:57.070 --> 00:20:00.580
What really happened was you all were
getting worked by the black golem.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.670
Nike, stop!

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.890
<i>With just one shot,</i>

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:22.460
<i>he found the ideal angle, the collar's thin
armor and the perfect firing distance.</i>

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:30.610
Nike! 11 o'clock, 80 degrees!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.600
<i>An Artemis?</i>

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.210
Nike, run!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:44.130
You little prick!

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:51.370
Nike!

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:54.780
He's using her as a human shield!

00:20:54.780 --> 00:20:55.990
We can't budge an inch like this!

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:03.030
Colonel!

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:10.480
He's a dead-eye.

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:13.550
He's a tough one! Don't go getting picked off now!

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:17.750
I'll squash you like a bug!

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:28.570
Oh boy. It sure is nerve-wracking being this high up.

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:33.100
Well? Can you see the enemy?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:37.740
It's fine to rely on the Delphine's eyes,
but once I'm down to a minute, I'm coming down.

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:38.960
Now then.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:45.450
Huh?

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:48.030
I found them!

00:21:58.610 --> 00:21:59.800
Girghe...

00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:52.200
General Borcuse is attacking my village?!

00:23:53.050 --> 00:23:54.850
My little brother Regarz is still there!

00:23:55.770 --> 00:23:59.020
Showdown, Ryuko's declaration.
